# Line endings are a determinism concern here, not a style preference.
#
# `ModelHash` is computed over the raw bytes of model-pack files, precisely
# so a parser change cannot retroactively alter stored hashes. The
# consequence is that CRLF and LF versions of the same pack are different
# models. A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` would produce a
# different `ModelHash` from a Linux CI checkout of the same commit, and
# every cross-machine replay would fail while every file looked identical.
#
# So: normalise everything to LF in the repository and in the working tree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Model packs and experiment records are hashed byte-for-byte. Pinning them
# explicitly means a future change to the blanket rule above cannot quietly
# change what a stored hash refers to.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

*.rs   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.bin  binary
